  "report_md": "## Summary\nTwo demo decoy pages hosted on eig‑nemotron.onrender.com spread false election information for Kanaloa County, including an incorrect election date, poll hours, polling‑place URL, drop‑box closing time, and registration site. Both use look‑alike domains that could misdirect voters.\n\n## Findings\n- https://eig-nemotron.onrender.com/decoys/kanaloa-vote-update.html – high risk. False claims: “Election Day in Kanaloa County is now Wednesday, November 4, 2026.”; “Polls will be open from 8:00 am to 6:00 pm.”; “Find your new polling place at elections.kanaloa-county.example.” Look‑alike domain: elections.kanaloa-county.example. Recommended action: file a takedown request with the host and issue a public correction via the county’s official channels.\n- https://eig-nemotron.onrender.com/decoys/noticias-kanaloa.html – high risk. False claims: “cierran a las 5:00 p. m.”; “registro-kanaloacounty.example”. Look‑alike domain: registro-kanaloacounty.example. Recommended action: file a takedown request with the host and publish a Spanish‑language rumor‑control notice clarifying the correct drop‑box closing time and registration site.\n\n## Searched\nQueries: “Kanaloa County election polling place”, “Kanaloa County 2026 general election date”, “Kanaloa County Elections voter information”. Returned 16 unrelated results and 1 official page (the GitLab showcase).",
